@* Drawer's Overview, written by hand after Dialog's, which it is: opening it (as a dialog), a form in
   a drawer previewed in each mode, edges and widths, a menu from the start edge, an action sheet, then what
   it shares with Dialog. Accessibility and See also come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A drawer is a panel that slides in from an edge of the screen, the end edge by default. It suits content that goes with the page rather than interrupting it, such as filters or a navigation menu. A drawer is a <Anchor Href="docs/components/dialog">Dialog</Anchor> with a different <Code>Placement</Code>, so everything a dialog does, it does too.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Opening the drawer</Heading>
<TextBlock>A drawer opens the same three ways as a dialog. For a button, add a <Code>DialogTrigger</Code> with the drawer's <Code>Id</Code>; for a link, add <Code>?dialog=</Code> and the id to the URL. From C#, set <Code>@@bind-Open</Code>.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>The trigger and the link work on <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">static pages</Anchor>, with JavaScript off too. <Anchor Href="docs/components/dialog#opening-the-dialog">Dialog's Overview</Anchor> shows each in every render mode.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">A form in a drawer</Heading>
<TextBlock>A drawer can contain a form, such as a list of filters, with its buttons at the bottom. Put a <Anchor Href="docs/components/form">Form</Anchor> in the drawer, with its fields in a <Code>DialogBody</Code> and its <Code>FormActions</Code> last. The body fills the drawer's height, so the buttons sit at its bottom as the footer and still submit the form.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="drawer-filters" />
<List>
    <ListItem>A form post on static pages closes the drawer.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>On interactive pages, the submit runs C# instead, so close the drawer there with <Code>@@bind-Open</Code>, as this example does.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>When a form post can fail, reopen the drawer with the errors, as in <Anchor Href="docs/components/dialog#a-form-in-a-dialog">A form in a dialog</Anchor>.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">Edges and widths</Heading>
<TextBlock>A drawer can open from any edge, at a width you choose. To set the width, set <Code>Size</Code> or <Code>Width</Code>. To open it from another edge, set <Code>Placement</Code>.</TextBlock>
<Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th><Code>Size</Code></th><th>Width</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><Code>Sm</Code></td><td>20rem</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>Md</Code> (default)</td><td>24rem</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>Lg</Code></td><td>32rem</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>Xl</Code></td><td>40rem</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>Full</Code></td><td>The full width</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</Prose>
<ExampleViewer Example="drawer-edges" />
<TextBlock><Code>Placement</Code> is <Code>End</Code> by default, or <Code>Start</Code>. <Code>Top</Code> and <Code>Bottom</Code> open a sheet as tall as its content, centered and 40rem wide at most, so it stays usable on a wide screen; on phones it spans the screen. For a sheet's width, <Code>Size</Code> is <Code>Sm</Code> 24rem, <Code>Md</Code> 40rem, <Code>Lg</Code> 48rem, <Code>Xl</Code> 64rem, or <Code>Full</Code> for the screen's width.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">A menu from the start edge</Heading>
<TextBlock>A drawer from the start edge suits navigation that slides in, such as a site's menu on phones. Set <Code>Placement="DialogPlacement.Start"</Code> and <Code>Size="DialogSize.Sm"</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="drawer-nav" />
<TextBlock>An app's navigation doesn't need a Drawer. In an <Anchor Href="docs/components/app-shell">AppShell</Anchor>, the <Anchor Href="docs/components/app-sidebar">AppSidebar</Anchor> becomes a drawer below its breakpoint by itself, opened by a <Code>SidebarToggle</Code>, with JavaScript off too.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">An action sheet</Heading>
<TextBlock>An action sheet offers a few actions on one thing, such as a photo, from the bottom of a phone's screen. Open a drawer from the bottom, put a full-width button per action in a form, and end with a <Code>DialogClose</Code> for Cancel. Choosing an action closes the sheet, as with a form in a drawer.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="drawer-action-sheet" />
<List>
    <ListItem>Keep the title: it names the sheet. Cancel does the close button's job, so <Code>ShowCloseButton="false"</Code> hides it.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>Mark a destructive action with <Code>Accent.Danger</Code>.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>For more than a handful of actions, or on wide screens, use a <Anchor Href="docs/components/menu">Menu</Anchor>.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">Header, footer and closing</Heading>
<TextBlock>Put the content in a <Code>DialogBody</Code> and the buttons in a <Code>DialogFooter</Code> after it. The body fills the drawer's height, so the footer sits at its bottom. Without a body, the footer follows the content partway down.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>Everything else works as on a dialog: <Code>Title</Code> or a <Code>DialogHeader</Code>, <Code>DialogClose</Code>, <Code>CloseOnBackdrop</Code>, <Code>ShowCloseButton</Code>, <Code>InsideForm</Code> and the close button's <Code>CloseLabel</Code>. <Anchor Href="docs/components/dialog">Dialog's Overview</Anchor> covers each.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <DialogTrigger For="filters">Filters</DialogTrigger>

        <Drawer Id="filters" Title="Filters" Size="DialogSize.Sm" @bind-Open="_open">
            <Form Model="Filters" FormName="filters" OnValidSubmit="ApplyAsync">
                <DialogBody Gap="5">
                    <RadioGroup @bind-Value="Filters!.Status" />
                </DialogBody>
                <FormActions>
                    <Button Submit>Apply</Button>
                </FormActions>
            </Form>
        </Drawer>

        @* ApplyAsync ends with _open = false, which closes it on an interactive page. *@
        """;
}
